the target language is: prolog.

the functions are:
    the num of years is *a number*.
    the salary is *a number*.

the templates are:
    the salary for *a number* is *a value* under table salary.

the table salary is, with all matches:
    num of years | value
    > 1          | 100
    > 2          | 200
    > 3          | 300
    > 5          | 500

the knowledge base n0116_count_collect_hitpolicy includes:

the text of the_model is at "sources/0116-count-collect-hitpolicy.dmn".

rule salary_1 with provenance the model at decision Salary:
the salary is a number N if
    N is the count of each V such that
        the num of years is a second number
        and the salary for the second number is a value V under table salary.

